// rule: SEM-2
// expect: run
// The core float primitives float.floor, ceil, trunc, round (ties away from
// zero), sqrt (correctly rounded) and abs at both widths, exactly: signed zeros,
// halves of both signs, the largest value below one half, the last binade with
// a fraction and the first without, subnormals, extremes, infinities and the NaN.
// Rows follow Rust coretests num/floats.rs (round, floor, ceil, trunc, abs,
// sqrt_domain) and Zig test/behavior/floatop.zig testSqrt; columns are the
// operand, then floor, ceil, trunc, round, sqrt and abs, as IEEE bits.
